# Files that must not go into the built cw4.apworld.
#
# Gitignore syntax. Archipelago reads this per world and appends it to
# data/GLOBAL.apignore, so everything that file already excludes
# (__pycache__, .DS_Store, /archipelago.json, /.git, /.gitignore) stays
# excluded and does not need repeating here.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. Until it did, the shipped .apworld carried the whole test
# suite: measured from the v0.1.10 artifact, cw4/test/ was 96,709 of 237,705
# uncompressed bytes - 41 percent of what every player downloads, to run code
# that only ever runs in CI. Nothing noticed, because nothing in the release
# path asserts anything about the .apworld's contents; tools/check_release.py
# now does.
#
# __pycache__ was already excluded, but by GLOBAL.apignore rather than by any
# decision made here - so the exclusion of test/ had simply never been
# considered. Note that the CI job builds the apworld with `zip -r ... -x
# '*/__pycache__/*'`, which hand-reimplements one line of the global file and
# honours none of this; that artifact is uploaded and never shipped.
/test/
